@model SlideViewModel

<section class="bullet-slide">
    <h1>Types Exist Whether You Acknowledge Them or Not</h1>

    <div class="row g-5 flex-grow-1 align-items-center">
        <div class="col-6">
            <ul class="slide-bullets">
                <li>
                    What is a <strong>number</strong>?
                </li>

                <li>
                    What is <code>null</code>?
                </li>

                <li>
                    Can values be <strong>coerced</strong>?
                </li>

                <li>
                    What does <code>+</code> mean?
                </li>

                <li>
                    What can functions <strong>accept and return</strong>?
                </li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="col-6">
            <ul class="slide-bullets">
                <li>
                    When do <strong>type errors</strong> happen?
                </li>

                <li>
                    Can types change?
                </li>

                <li>
                    Do your types exist in the
                    <strong>implementing language or runtime</strong>?
                </li>

                <li>
                    Do your users need to know?
                </li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-4 p-3 rounded text-center bg-body-tertiary">
        <span class="fs-3">
            Ignoring the type system does not mean you don't have one.
            <strong>It means it's implicit.</strong>
        </span>
    </div>
</section>